# HTTP client

HTTP/1.1 requests from a LOGOS program — the client half that `http.lg`'s server half pairs with —
written in LOGOS over the socket natives, the way `postgres.lg` speaks its protocol. An `https://`
URL is reached through `tcpConnectTls`, which verifies the server's certificate against the bundled
roots (and `LOGOS_TLS_EXTRA_ROOT`); an `http://` URL through `tcpConnect`.

Every request is bounded. `timeoutMs` is the deadline for the whole exchange — connecting, sending
and reading the reply — and a reply larger than `httpMaxReplyBytes()` is refused rather than held.
A request asks the server to close the connection when it has answered (`Connection: close`) and
asks for the body as it is (`Accept-Encoding: identity`), so a reply is read once and nothing is
left open behind it.

A reply's body is delimited the three ways HTTP/1.1 allows: by `Content-Length`, by chunked
transfer coding (decoded here, trailers ignored), or by the server closing the connection. A body
that ends short of its own framing is an `Err`, never a silently truncated `Ok`.

What a program gets back is the status, the reason phrase, the headers — names lower-cased, a
repeated header's values joined with `, ` — and the body. A non-2xx status is still an `Ok`: the
server answered, and what the answer means is the caller's to decide. `Err` means no answer arrived.

## Note
Where a URL points: whether it is secured, the host, the port, and the request target (the path
with its query, always starting with `/`).

## A HttpUrl has:
    a secure, which is Bool.
    a host, which is Text.
    a port, which is Int.
    a target, which is Text.

## Note
A server's answer.

## A HttpReply has:
    a status, which is Int.
    a reason, which is Text.
    a headers, which is Map of Text to Text.
    a body, which is Text.

## Note
The largest reply a request reads: 256 MiB. A server that sends more is refused, so a reply can
never exhaust the program's memory by being large.

## To httpMaxReplyBytes () -> Int:
    Return 268435456.

## Note
Splits an `http://` or `https://` URL into where it points.

Credentials inside the URL (`user:pass@host`) are refused, because a URL is logged and displayed far
more often than it is kept secret — credentials travel in a header. A fragment (`#…`) never reaches
the wire.

## To httpParseUrl (url: Text) -> Result of HttpUrl and Text:
    Let mutable secure be false.
    Let mutable rest be "".
    Let mutable known be false.
    If startsWith(url, "https://"):
        Set secure to true.
        Set rest to removePrefix(url, "https://").
        Set known to true.
    If startsWith(url, "http://"):
        Set rest to removePrefix(url, "http://").
        Set known to true.
    If known is equal to false:
        Return a new Err with error "httpRequest: the url must start with http:// or https://, got {url}".
    Set rest to cutBefore(rest, "#").
    Let rb be text_bytes(rest).
    Let n be length of rb.
    Let mutable authority be a new Seq of Int.
    Let mutable targetB be a new Seq of Int.
    Let mutable inTarget be false.
    Let mutable i be 1.
    While i is at most n:
        Let b be item i of rb.
        If inTarget is equal to false and (b is equal to 47 or b is equal to 63):
            Set inTarget to true.
            If b is equal to 63:
                Push 47 to targetB.
        If inTarget:
            Push b to targetB.
        Otherwise:
            Push b to authority.
        Set i to i + 1.
    If length of targetB is equal to 0:
        Push 47 to targetB.
    Let hostPort be text_from_bytes(authority).
    If indexOf(hostPort, "@") is greater than 0:
        Return a new Err with error "httpRequest: credentials in the url are refused; send them in a header".
    If startsWith(hostPort, "["):
        Return a new Err with error "httpRequest: a bracketed IPv6 host is not supported, got {hostPort}".
    Let mutable hostVal be hostPort.
    Let mutable portVal be 80.
    If secure:
        Set portVal to 443.
    If indexOf(hostPort, ":") is greater than 0:
        Set hostVal to cutBefore(hostPort, ":").
        Let portText be cutAfter(hostPort, ":").
        If allDigits(portText) is equal to false:
            Return a new Err with error "httpRequest: the port must be a number, got {portText}".
        Set portVal to parseInt(portText).
        If portVal is less than 1 or portVal is greater than 65535:
            Return a new Err with error "httpRequest: the port must be between 1 and 65535, got {portVal}".
    If hostVal is equal to "":
        Return a new Err with error "httpRequest: the url has no host, got {url}".
    Return a new Ok with value (a new HttpUrl with secure secure and host hostVal and port portVal and target (text_from_bytes(targetB))).

## Note
The bytes of one request: its line, `Host`, the framing headers, the caller's headers and the body.

`Host` carries the port when it is not the scheme's default. A caller's header that names the
framing — `Host`, `Content-Length`, `Transfer-Encoding`, `Connection` — is refused: the client owns
those, and a second, disagreeing copy is how a request is smuggled.

## To httpRequestBytes (method: Text) and (u: HttpUrl) and (headers: Map of Text to Text) and (body: Text) -> Result of Seq of Int and Text:
    If isHeaderName(method) is equal to false:
        Return a new Err with error "httpRequest: the method is not a valid token, got {method}".
    Let mutable hostHeader be u's host.
    Let defaultPort be 80.
    If u's secure:
        If u's port is not 443:
            Set hostHeader to "{u's host}:{u's port}".
    Otherwise:
        If u's port is not defaultPort:
            Set hostHeader to "{u's host}:{u's port}".
    Let bodyBytes be text_bytes(body).
    Let mutable head be "{method} {u's target} HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: {hostHeader}\r\nUser-Agent: logos-httpclient/1\r\nAccept-Encoding: identity\r\nConnection: close\r\n".
    If length of bodyBytes is greater than 0 or method is equal to "POST" or method is equal to "PUT" or method is equal to "PATCH":
        Set head to head + "Content-Length: {length of bodyBytes}\r\n".
    Repeat for (name, value) in headers:
        If isHeaderName(name) is equal to false:
            Return a new Err with error "httpRequest: header name is not a valid token, got {name}".
        If isHeaderValue(value) is equal to false:
            Return a new Err with error "httpRequest: header {name} holds a forbidden control byte".
        Let low be lower(name).
        If low is equal to "host" or low is equal to "content-length" or low is equal to "transfer-encoding" or low is equal to "connection":
            Return a new Err with error "httpRequest: the client owns the {name} header".
        Set head to head + "{name}: {value}\r\n".
    Set head to head + "\r\n".
    Let mutable out be text_bytes(head).
    Repeat for b in bodyBytes:
        Push b to out.
    Return a new Ok with value out.

## Note
Where the header block ends in `buf`: the 1-based index of the first byte after the blank line,
or 0 while the blank line has not arrived.

## To httpHeadEnd (buf: Seq of Int) -> Int:
    Let at be bytesIndexSub(buf, [13, 10, 13, 10]).
    If at is equal to 0:
        Return 0.
    Return at + 4.

## Note
The status line and headers of a reply, from the bytes before the blank line: the status, the
reason phrase and the header map (lower-cased names, repeated values joined with `, `).

## To httpParseHead (buf: Seq of Int) and (bodyAt: Int) -> Result of HttpReply and Text:
    Let mutable headB be a new Seq of Int.
    Let mutable i be 1.
    While i is less than bodyAt - 4:
        Push item i of buf to headB.
        Set i to i + 1.
    Let headText be text_from_bytes(headB).
    Let headLines be split(headText, "\r\n").
    If length of headLines is equal to 0:
        Return a new Err with error "httpRequest: the reply has no status line".
    Let statusLine be item 1 of headLines.
    If startsWith(statusLine, "HTTP/1.") is equal to false:
        Return a new Err with error "httpRequest: the reply is not HTTP/1.x: {statusLine}".
    Let afterVersion be cutAfter(statusLine, " ").
    Let codeText be cutBefore(afterVersion, " ").
    If allDigits(codeText) is equal to false or length of text_bytes(codeText) is not 3:
        Return a new Err with error "httpRequest: the status code is malformed: {statusLine}".
    Let mutable reasonText be "".
    If indexOf(afterVersion, " ") is greater than 0:
        Set reasonText to cutAfter(afterVersion, " ").
    Let mutable hs be a new Map of Text to Text.
    Let mutable k be 2.
    While k is at most length of headLines:
        Let line be item k of headLines.
        If indexOf(line, ":") is equal to 0:
            Return a new Err with error "httpRequest: a reply header has no colon: {line}".
        Let name be lower(trim(cutBefore(line, ":"))).
        Let value be trim(cutAfter(line, ":")).
        If hs contains name:
            Set item name of hs to (item name of hs) + ", " + value.
        Otherwise:
            Set item name of hs to value.
        Set k to k + 1.
    Return a new Ok with value (a new HttpReply with status (parseInt(codeText)) and reason reasonText and headers hs and body "").

## Note
Decodes a chunked body that starts at 1-based `at` in `buf`.

`Ok` carries the body once the final zero-size chunk has arrived; `Err` with the text `incomplete`
means more bytes are needed; any other `Err` is a malformed body.

## To httpDechunk (buf: Seq of Int) and (at: Int) -> Result of Seq of Int and Text:
    Let n be length of buf.
    Let mutable out be a new Seq of Int.
    Let mutable i be at.
    While true:
        Let mutable size be 0.
        Let mutable digits be 0.
        Let mutable sizing be true.
        While sizing:
            If i is greater than n:
                Return a new Err with error "incomplete".
            Let b be item i of buf.
            Let isHex be (b is at least 48 and b is at most 57) or (b is at least 97 and b is at most 102) or (b is at least 65 and b is at most 70).
            If isHex:
                Set size to size * 16 + byteHexVal(b).
                Set digits to digits + 1.
                If size is greater than httpMaxReplyBytes():
                    Return a new Err with error "httpRequest: a chunk is larger than the reply limit".
                Set i to i + 1.
            Otherwise:
                Set sizing to false.
        If digits is equal to 0:
            Return a new Err with error "httpRequest: a chunk size is malformed".
        Let mutable seekingEnd be true.
        While seekingEnd:
            If i + 1 is greater than n:
                Return a new Err with error "incomplete".
            If item i of buf is equal to 13 and item (i + 1) of buf is equal to 10:
                Set i to i + 2.
                Set seekingEnd to false.
            Otherwise:
                Set i to i + 1.
        If size is equal to 0:
            Return a new Ok with value out.
        If i + size + 1 is greater than n:
            Return a new Err with error "incomplete".
        Let mutable j be 0.
        While j is less than size:
            Push item (i + j) of buf to out.
            Set j to j + 1.
        Set i to i + size.
        If item i of buf is not 13 or item (i + 1) of buf is not 10:
            Return a new Err with error "httpRequest: a chunk does not end with CRLF".
        Set i to i + 2.
    Return a new Err with error "incomplete".

## Note
Sends one request and reads its reply, under one deadline for the whole exchange.

## To httpRequest (method: Text) and (url: Text) and (headers: Map of Text to Text) and (body: Text) and (timeoutMs: Int) -> Result of HttpReply and Text:
    If timeoutMs is less than 1:
        Return a new Err with error "httpRequest: timeoutMs must be positive, got {timeoutMs}".
    Let started be now().
    Inspect httpParseUrl(url):
        When Err (why):
            Return a new Err with error why.
        When Ok (u):
            Inspect httpRequestBytes(method, u, headers, body):
                When Err (why):
                    Return a new Err with error why.
                When Ok (wire):
                    Inspect httpOpen(u):
                        When Err (why):
                            Return a new Err with error "httpRequest: cannot connect to {u's host}:{u's port}: {why}".
                        When Ok (c):
                            Let answer be httpExchange(c, wire, method, started, timeoutMs).
                            Let closed be tcpClose(c).
                            Return answer.

## Note
Opens the connection a URL names: TLS for `https://`, plain TCP for `http://` — exactly one of
them, so a secured URL is never first tried in the clear.

## To httpOpen (u: HttpUrl) -> Result of Int and Text:
    If u's secure:
        Return tcpConnectTls(u's host, u's port).
    Return tcpConnect(u's host, u's port).

## Note
The exchange on an open connection: send the request, then read until the reply's framing says it
is complete (or the server closes), checking the deadline before every read.

## To httpExchange (c: Int) and (wire: Seq of Int) and (method: Text) and (started: Int) and (timeoutMs: Int) -> Result of HttpReply and Text:
    Let armed be tcpSetTimeout(c, timeoutMs).
    Inspect tcpSend(c, wire):
        When Err (why):
            Return a new Err with error "httpRequest: cannot send the request: {why}".
        When Ok (sent):
            Let ignored be sent.
    Let mutable buf be a new Seq of Int.
    Let mutable bodyAt be 0.
    Let mutable reading be true.
    Let mutable closedByServer be false.
    Let mutable parsed be a new HttpReply with status 0 and reason "" and headers (a new Map of Text to Text) and body "".
    While reading:
        If now() - started is greater than timeoutMs:
            Return a new Err with error "httpRequest: no complete reply within {timeoutMs} ms".
        Inspect tcpRecv(c, 65536):
            When Err (why):
                Return a new Err with error "httpRequest: reading the reply failed: {why}".
            When Ok (piece):
                If length of piece is equal to 0:
                    Set closedByServer to true.
                    Set reading to false.
                Repeat for b in piece:
                    Push b to buf.
        If length of buf is greater than httpMaxReplyBytes():
            Return a new Err with error "httpRequest: the reply is larger than {httpMaxReplyBytes()} bytes".
        If bodyAt is equal to 0:
            Set bodyAt to httpHeadEnd(buf).
            If bodyAt is greater than 0:
                Inspect httpParseHead(buf, bodyAt):
                    When Err (why):
                        Return a new Err with error why.
                    When Ok (h):
                        Set parsed to h.
        If bodyAt is greater than 0:
            Inspect httpBodyIfComplete(buf, bodyAt, parsed, method, closedByServer):
                When Ok (done):
                    Return a new Ok with value done.
                When Err (why):
                    If why is not "incomplete":
                        Return a new Err with error why.
        If closedByServer and bodyAt is equal to 0:
            Return a new Err with error "httpRequest: the server closed the connection before the reply's headers ended".
    Return a new Err with error "httpRequest: the server closed the connection before the reply was complete".

## Note
The reply with its body, once `buf` holds all of it: `Err` with the text `incomplete` while more
is owed. A reply to `HEAD`, a 1xx, a 204 and a 304 carry no body whatever their headers say.

## To httpBodyIfComplete (buf: Seq of Int) and (bodyAt: Int) and (h: HttpReply) and (method: Text) and (closed: Bool) -> Result of HttpReply and Text:
    Let st be h's status.
    If method is equal to "HEAD" or st is less than 200 or st is equal to 204 or st is equal to 304:
        Return a new Ok with value h.
    Let hs be h's headers.
    Let n be length of buf.
    If hs contains "transfer-encoding":
        Let coding be item "transfer-encoding" of hs.
        If lower(coding) is not "chunked":
            Return a new Err with error "httpRequest: transfer coding {coding} is not supported".
        Inspect httpDechunk(buf, bodyAt):
            When Ok (bodyB):
                Return a new Ok with value (a new HttpReply with status st and reason (h's reason) and headers hs and body (text_from_bytes(bodyB))).
            When Err (why):
                If why is equal to "incomplete" and closed:
                    Return a new Err with error "httpRequest: the connection closed inside a chunked body".
                Return a new Err with error why.
    If hs contains "content-length":
        Let lenText be trim(item "content-length" of hs).
        If allDigits(lenText) is equal to false:
            Return a new Err with error "httpRequest: Content-Length is malformed: {lenText}".
        Let want be parseInt(lenText).
        If want is greater than httpMaxReplyBytes():
            Return a new Err with error "httpRequest: the reply is larger than {httpMaxReplyBytes()} bytes".
        Let have be n - bodyAt + 1.
        If have is less than want:
            If closed:
                Return a new Err with error "httpRequest: the connection closed after {have} of {want} body bytes".
            Return a new Err with error "incomplete".
        Let mutable bodyB be a new Seq of Int.
        Let mutable i be bodyAt.
        While i is less than bodyAt + want:
            Push item i of buf to bodyB.
            Set i to i + 1.
        Return a new Ok with value (a new HttpReply with status st and reason (h's reason) and headers hs and body (text_from_bytes(bodyB))).
    If closed:
        Let mutable rest be a new Seq of Int.
        Let mutable i be bodyAt.
        While i is at most n:
            Push item i of buf to rest.
            Set i to i + 1.
        Return a new Ok with value (a new HttpReply with status st and reason (h's reason) and headers hs and body (text_from_bytes(rest))).
    Return a new Err with error "incomplete".

## Note
A `GET` with no body.

## To httpGet (url: Text) and (headers: Map of Text to Text) and (timeoutMs: Int) -> Result of HttpReply and Text:
    Return httpRequest("GET", url, headers, "", timeoutMs).

## Note
A `POST` of a JSON document, with `Content-Type: application/json` added unless the caller named
a content type.

## To httpPostJson (url: Text) and (headers: Map of Text to Text) and (body: Text) and (timeoutMs: Int) -> Result of HttpReply and Text:
    Let mutable hs be a new Map of Text to Text.
    Let mutable typed be false.
    Repeat for (k, v) in headers:
        Set item k of hs to v.
        If lower(k) is equal to "content-type":
            Set typed to true.
    If typed is equal to false:
        Set item "Content-Type" of hs to "application/json".
    Return httpRequest("POST", url, hs, body, timeoutMs).
